# Project intent

`app/main.py` is designed to be user friendly and novice editable: categories, `Patch(...).add(...)` lists, and `AppConfig` rack indexes. Do not move that catalog into the package. Keep the sequential `.add` style and the existing explanatory comments.

Implementation lives under `app/carla_interface/`. Avoid giant god files; split modules by responsibility when a file grows unwieldy. `os/` is the piano-PC overlay (autostart, JACK, Carla project) — leave it alone unless asked.

Runtime is Linux (`oscsend`, `aplaymidi`). Do not reintroduce Windows code paths.

# Agent UI preview

This is a PyQt6 kiosk, not a browser app. After UI changes, grab a PNG and Read it — do not skip visual check.

1. Use `app/.venv` (Python 3.10 + `requirements.txt`). Create if missing:
   `py -3.10 -m venv .venv` then `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt` from `app/`.
2. Never set `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`. Fonts tofu or garble. Leave the default Windows Qt plugin.
3. Keep the grabber out of the repo. Temp script: put `app/` on `sys.path`, replace `carla_interface.run_app` and `carla_interface.runtime.run_app` with a function that waits ~500ms, `grab()`s the visible top-level widget, writes `%TEMP%\carla_interface_preview.png`, then `app.quit()`. Monkeypatch `QWidget.showMaximized` to `setGeometry(80, 80, 1600, 900)` + `show()` so the frameless window does not cover the desktop. `import runpy; runpy.run_path(..., run_name="__main__")` on `app/main.py`.
4. Run with `app/.venv/Scripts/python.exe`, then Read the PNG.
5. `oscsend` / `aplaymidi` already no-op on failure — Carla is not required to preview.

Human launch from `app/`: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py`. Ctrl+C quits.
